<title>GREECE: GREEK INFLATION EDGES UP TO 5.5 PCT YR/YR IN JUNE.</title>
<headline>GREEK INFLATION EDGES UP TO 5.5 PCT YR/YR IN JUNE.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek consumer price inflation edged up to 5.5 percent year-on-year in June from 5.4 percent in May, the National Statistics Service (NSS) said.</p>
<p>A recent Reuters poll of 15 bankers and economists produced a mean forecast of 5.4 percent for June inflation. Forecasts ranged from 5.4 to 5.6 percent.</p>
<p>    Consumer Price Index     June 97     May 97	  June 96</p>
<p>    Month-on-month		 0.4%	  0.4%	   0.3%</p>
<p>    Year-on-year		   5.5%	  5.4%	   8.4%</p>
<p>    Index (1994=100)	   125.5	 125.0	  118.9</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
